        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0c9bf5b5-3628-5407-9112-7ae526cefac1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Pocahontas, The Game Plan, The Little Mermaid, Aladdin, Dinosaur, Home on the Range, The Prince and the Pauper, Rush Hour 2, Boat Trip, Act of Valor\n- People: H. Lee Peterson, Roselyn Sánchez, Andy Fickman, Nichole Millard, Kathryn Price, Audrey Wells, Dwayne Johnson\n- Companies: Walt Disney Feature Animation, Walt Disney Pictures\n- Roles: film editor, assistant editor, director, writer, actor\n\nFacts:\n- Pocahontas is a 1995 American animated musical romantic-comedy-drama film produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation for Walt Disney Pictures.\n- H. Lee Peterson was an assistant editor for The Little Mermaid for Walt Disney Pictures.\n- H. Lee Peterson was the lead film editor for Aladdin for Walt Disney Pictures.\n- H. Lee Peterson was the lead film editor for Pocahontas for Walt Disney Pictures.\n- Roselyn Sánchez appeared in Rush Hour 2 in 2001.\n- Roselyn Sánchez appeared in Boat Trip in 2002.\n- H. Lee Peterson was the lead film editor for Dinosaur for Walt Disney Pictures.\n- H. Lee Peterson was the lead film editor for Home on the Range for Walt Disney Pictures.\n- The Game Plan is a 2007 American family comedy film directed by Andy Fickman, written by Nichole Millard, Kathryn Price, and Audrey Wells, and starring Dwayne Johnson.\n- The Game Plan was the last film in which Dwayne Johnson was billed as \"The Rock.\"\n- Roselyn Sánchez appeared in The Game Plan in 2007.\n- Roselyn Sánchez appeared in Act of Valor in 2012.\n- H. Lee Peterson was the lead film editor for the short film The Prince and the Pauper starring Mickey Mouse for Walt Disney Pictures.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "21b40460-199d-5f1d-b678-922b303d72f8",
        "text": "Page: Pocahontas (1995 film). Sentence: Pocahontas is a 1995 American animated musical romantic-comedy-drama film produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation for Walt Disney Pictures.\nPage: The Game Plan (film). Sentence: The Game Plan is a 2007 American family comedy film directed by Andy Fickman and written by Nichole Millard, Kathryn Price and Audrey Wells and starring Dwayne \"The Rock\" Johnson (marking the last film in which Johnson uses his ring name \"The Rock\" in billing).\nPage: H. Lee Peterson. Sentence: His credits for Walt Disney Pictures include being an assistant editor for \"The Little Mermaid\", and the lead film editor for \"Aladdin\", \"Pocahontas\", \"Dinosaur\", \"Home on the Range\" and the short film \"The Prince and the Pauper; starring Mickey Mouse\".\nPage: Roselyn Sánchez. Sentence: In film, Sánchez has appeared in \"Rush Hour 2\" (2001), \"Boat Trip\" (2002), \"The Game Plan\" (2007), and \"Act of Valor\" (2012).",
